sequenceDiagram
    participant N1 as Node 1
    participant N2 as Node 2
    participant N3 as Node 3

    Note over N1, N3: 0 - Initialize: W_active = W_anchor = W_mix (identical on all nodes)

    par
        Note over N1, N3: 1 - Distributed training
        N1->>N1: Update W_active with gradients
        N2->>N2: Update W_active with gradients
        N3->>N3: Update W_active with gradients
    end

    rect rgba(200, 180, 255, 0.1)
        Note over N1, N3: 2 - Sync interval hit (every node, in parallel)
        N1->>N1: Mix: W_active += γ(W_mix - W_anchor)
        N1->>N1: D1 = top_k(W_active - W_anchor), W_anchor += D1, W_mix += w11·D1
        N1->>N2: Send D1 (1->2)
        N1->>N3: Send D1 (1->3)
        N2->>N2: W_mix += w21·D1
        N3->>N3: W_mix += w31·D1
        Note over N2, N3: Nodes 2 and 3 do the same with D2 and D3
    end

    Note over N1, N3: 3 - Continue distributed training until the next sync interval
